# This repo is the SOURCE that builds the game, not the build. Anything the
# pipeline can regenerate, and anything that is a copy of something else, stays
# out — the tree on disk is ~550 MB and all but a few MB of that is derived,
# archived or duplicated.

# The site is no longer a separate repo. index.html, game.html, style.css and
# the customizer copies at the ROOT are the published surface, tracked on
# purpose: they are what GitHub Pages serves. Everything under game/ is the
# source they are built from.

# Checkpoint copies of ice_hockey.html. 47 MB of near-identical 3 MB files.
# The retired SCRIPTS in there are kept: the docs point at them by name, and a
# clone with a dangling reference to fit3.py is worse than 20 KB of dead code.
# (Ignoring the directory itself would make these negations unreachable.)
/game/backups/*
!/game/backups/*.py
!/game/backups/*superseded*
*.bak_*

# Generated by the pipeline. measure_photo -> fit_photo -> rectify -> boards ->
# make25d rebuilds every one of these from the reference picture, byte for byte;
# they were verified identical across a rerun before this line was written.
/game/ice_hockey_25d.html
/game/rink_mask.png
/game/rink_boards.png
/game/_ih25shot.html
/game/_ih25probe.html
/game/_simprobe.html

# Probe output: screenshots and overlays, regenerated by ih25_shot.sh and
# overlay_check.py on demand.
/game/*.png
# Binary assets and archives that are inputs to other work, not to this
# pipeline: models, Blender files, captured video, the NHL 25 reference dump and
# the forked build this one came from.
/assets/
/legacy/
# tools/ is ignored for its BINARY working files (armlen, regrip), not as a
# rule about the folder — a script that belongs to the repo is re-included by
# name. This has to be /tools/* rather than /tools/, because git cannot
# re-include anything inside an excluded DIRECTORY.
/tools/*
!/tools/menu_probe.sh
/armtest/
/reference/*
!/reference/rink_reference_2026-08-13.png
!/reference/RINK_IMAGE_PROMPT.md
# The menu's locker-room backdrop, kept for the same reason as the rink
# picture above: img/locker-room.jpg is DERIVED from it (one PIL call, recipe
# in reference/LOCKER_ROOM_IMAGE.md) and an irreplaceable input that lives only
# in ~/Lataukset cannot be rebuilt from a clone.
!/reference/locker_room_reference_2026-08-15.png
!/reference/LOCKER_ROOM_IMAGE.md

__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Pre-change backups live alongside the real files. They must never be
# committed, and while untracked they bury genuine changes in git status, which
# is exactly the noise that let a stale deploy go unnoticed three times.
*.bak_pre_*
*.bak

# Probe and harness scratch. Vendored CDN copies of three.js get dropped next
# to the page when testing headlessly; they are not part of the site.
__probe*.html
/three.min.js
/GLTFLoader.js
